{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQ8FE9uqHaCAP5dh2ty8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Oracle (ORCL) effective tax rate, fiscal year ended May 31, 2024**\n\n**KPI: Effective tax rate**\n- FY2024 (ended 5/31/2024): **10.9%**\n- FY2023 (ended 5/31/2023): **6.8%**\n- **Delta: +410bps** (10.9% − 6.8%)\n\n**KPI: Income tax expense (supporting figure)**\n- FY2024: **$1,274 million**\n- FY2023: **$623 million**\n- Change: +$651 million, about 104% higher\n\nThe rate went up because tax expense roughly doubled, which outpaced the growth in pre-tax income. I didn't pull pre-tax income for these years directly. Dividing tax expense by the rate puts it at about $11.7B for FY2024, but that's a derived estimate, not a reported figure. I also didn't get the filing's explanation of the rate change, such as discrete items or changes in the earnings mix by jurisdiction.\n\nThe tool also returned data from 10-Ks filed after 16 May 2025. I ignored those; they show the same FY2024 and FY2023 rates.\n\n**Sources**\n- Oracle Corporation Form 10-K for FY2024, filed 2024-06-20, accession 0000950170-24-075605 (FY2024 and FY2023 rate and tax expense)\n- Oracle Corporation Form 10-K for FY2023, filed 2023-06-20, accession 0000950170-23-028914 (confirms the FY2023 rate of 6.8% and tax expense of $623M)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3573,"cache_read_input_tokens":7776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3573},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"426d824f-25d2-4274-9930-f5de0a3ee176","uuid":"e4b48c20-ca00-4dd3-969a-a61d2434925a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T03:18:43.077Z","request_id":"req_011CgQ8FDnaZo5YXrouM8Ngu"}
